{"agent_id":"pp3g-6noj-fix-test-the-fetch-mcp-server-uvx-mcp-server-fetch","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-05T23:37:55.375395620Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3a7e8d4a-fb0b-4659-978b-4ee0ec1258c1","comment_uuid":"8d441a72-b0fd-403a-8512-95e984930edc","author":"pp3g-6noj-fix-test-the-fetch-mcp-server-uvx-mcp-server-fetch","content":"Plan: (1) FIX root cause identified — uvx resolves mcp-server-fetch==2026.7.10 which requires mcp>=1.1.3, but uvx also resolves mcp==2.0.0 (latest). mcp SDK 2.x renamed/removed McpError from mcp.shared.exceptions, so fetch's server.py ImportError on startup → 'server unavailable key=fetch' every launch. Fix: pin mcp SDK <2.0 in the uvx command (uvx --with 'mcp<2.0' mcp-server-fetch) so the ephemeral env satisfies the package's >=1.1.3 constraint with a 1.x SDK where McpError exists. Verified process-level: initialize + tools/list handshake succeeds with the pin; fails without it. Will update ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json, re-verify with a real tools/call fetch, then (2) TEST token savings: fetch same URL via MCP tool vs curl raw HTML, estimate input tokens (markdown vs HTML), compare content quality, post verdict + restart requirement (fix takes effect next opencode launch).","created_at":"2026-08-05T23:37:55.367388412Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:qq8WMXw27tnrgF9BEg0uw+3ZAAEJMBjh6n/pgzv6lnQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgfkMq22EekZcloHYBuYOsrIlERFGflIrs2/zWogPAEy0AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAmyUOJg85Cfw6z09pFUUd9zPJon7C+zgQXh9X3IdOuz1QbxaVHkUSaAwjOfmggLOQbmcEdkTaSLfTD7BUmixCAQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:qq8WMXw27tnrgF9BEg0uw+3ZAAEJMBjh6n/pgzv6lnQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgfkMq22EekZcloHYBuYOsrIlERFGflIrs2/zWogPAEy0AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA9DieqSgxIZIU4DBaSdNun7NeKoFap8nS4xOrvvsgBuNr59bX4Z5Jyj2QOoY4C3Q3SfOLqAl9cJRyPE+1EdfAA="}
